          "location": "orientation[6].text; retrieval_prompts[12].answer",
          "problem": "The section paraphrases the lock box sign as one 'stating in legible print that lock boxes for securing prescription medications are available at the pharmacy'. M.G.L. c. 94C, s. 21B(b)(ii) requires the sign to include a prescribed statement ('...your prescription medications are available at this pharmacy'), not any wording to that effect.",
          "rationale": "One learning objective is the wording of the sign, and the statute fixes it as 'the following statement' in legibly printed font. A paraphrase that drops 'your' and turns 'this pharmacy' into 'the pharmacy', with no quotation marks, suggests that any equivalent wording complies. A candidate or pharmacy relying on it could pick or post non-conforming wording. Size (at least 4 by 5 inches), placement (on or near the pharmacy counter), the covered pharmacies and the institutional exclusion are all stated correctly. Fix: quote the statutory statement verbatim.",
