      "practice_mapping_verdict": "PASS",
      "summary": "Checked against current official text: 247 CMR 9.02, 9.04(4), (9), (11), (15) and 9.09; Policy 2021-02; the delivery and shipping advisory; M.G.L. c. 94C, s. 21B; Circular Letters DHCQ 18-6-679 and 20-3-700; and 21 CFR 1300.01, 1301.13(e), 1301.76(b), (d), 1304.05, 1305.03(d), 1306.05(f), 1306.06, 1306.11(d)(5), 1306.14(b), 1306.15, 1306.24(b), 1306.26(g) and 1306.27. 105 CMR 150.008(E) was checked through the LII transcription because the official PDF's text layer cannot be extracted. The substantive teaching is accurate. 9.02(3) is correctly limited to controlled substances. The advisory is correctly presented as best-practice recommendations, apart from the binding regulation. The central fill destination, licensure, Schedule VI (gabapentin) carve-out and compounding bar match Policy IV(b). The federal marking, transmission, retention, label, partner-list, oral-CII, Form 222 and in-transit-loss rules are assigned to the correct pharmacy. The gap between 9.04(11) and the policy's licensure requirement is handled in common_traps[3]. LTCF and hospice caps, sealing, the 48-hour reseal, ownership and reconciliation match the sources, and the unbanded bed counts (50; 10 and 21) are disclosed with a conservative course. All 15 practice questions are answerable from the section, and none of their keys or explanations is contradicted. One Low defect: the lock box sign's mandatory statement is paraphrased rather than quoted. MINOR_EDIT to quote it verbatim."
